body+=section('One family shows why the suffix matters','<p>MS51830 keylocking inserts distinguish material, coating and internal locking options within a single series. Revision G includes CA for A286 and QX for zinc-nickel plated alloy steel. Its L and LM locking suffixes distinguish aerospace and non-aerospace lubrication requirements.</p><p>Those codes belong to that series. They should not be copied into other MS, NAS or AN part numbers as universal material or finish rules.</p>'+chips([('MS51830 thread and designation guide','Reference-MS51830.html')]),'SERIES-SPECIFIC EXAMPLE')
body+=section('Questions to resolve before changing a finish','<ul class="ref-list"><li>Does the drawing permit an alternative material or coating?</li><li>Does the proposed part preserve dimensions, thread fit and specified performance?</li><li>Are application-specific lubrication or locking requirements retained?</li><li>Will the required certificates and processing records be available?</li><li>Who must approve the change before purchase?</li></ul><p>If a finish is difficult to source, ask Webson to review the exact requirement. Any proposed alternative should be identified separately for the appropriate approval.</p>'+chips([('Prepare a complete RFQ','Resources-Mil-Spec-RFQ-Checklist.html'),('Questions about alternatives','Resources-Mil-Spec-Purchasing-FAQ.html')]),'DISCUSS THE REQUIREMENT')
